course: dictionary
lesson: 14982
title: Repelling: pushing away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Repelling means pushing something away or keeping it away. It comes from the verb repel, which means to push back. «The raincoat was good at repelling the rain, so Sam stayed dry.» The rain could not get in, because the coat pushed it away.
explain: Scientists use this word too. «Two south poles of magnets were repelling each other, so they pushed apart.» Like poles repel, and unlike poles attract. You can feel this push if you hold two magnets close together.
explain: Repelling can also mean fighting something off. «The soldiers spent the night repelling the attackers at the castle gate.» Clues like soldiers, attackers and castle tell you the soldiers were keeping the enemy out. Ask yourself: is something being pushed away, or fought off?
fact: Repelling means pushing something away or keeping it away.
fact: «Repelling» is the -ing form of the verb «repel»: repel, repels, repelled, repelling.
fact: In science, like poles of magnets repel, and unlike poles attract.
fact: «Repelling an attack» means fighting it off.
fact: Something repelling can also cause disgust, but «repellent» or «repulsive» is more common for that meaning.
exercise: «The waterproof coat was good at repelling the rain.» What is the coat doing to the rain? | *Pushing it away | Making it stronger | Singing to it | Drinking it up
exercise: Two north poles of magnets push each other apart. Which word describes this push? | *Repelling | Attracting | Sleeping | Shining
exercise: «The soldiers were busy repelling the attackers at the gate.» What does repelling mean here? | Counting them | Feeding them | Inviting them in | *Fighting them off
test: «Insect spray works by ___ mosquitoes.» Which word fits best? | Attracting | *Repelling | Feeding | Counting
test: «The castle walls were built for ___ attackers.» Which word fits best? | Inviting | *Repelling | Hiding | Painting
exam: Two south poles of magnets facing each other are ___ each other. Which word fits best? | Joining | *Repelling | Ignoring | Attracting
